    {
     "q": "Can we release water on online TOC and conductivity?",
     "a": "For those two, yes, when the instruments are qualified and the sample point represents the water used. Microbial counts and endotoxin stay laboratory tests."
    },
    {
     "q": "Our transmitters show compensated conductivity. Is that a problem?",
     "a": "For trending, no. USP <645> stage 1 uses the raw reading against the table row for the measured temperature. Compensation can pass water stage 1 would fail. We store both."
    },
    {
     "q": "Is your system Part 11 compliant?",
     "a": "No system is on its own; your site is, by controls plus procedures. Our Part 11 and Annex 11 assessment shows which clauses need a site procedure."
    },
    {
     "q": "Do we get full access to the PLC and HMI code?",
     "a": "[code delivered unlocked, and who owns it] The version and checksum seen at FAT are recorded, so you can show the running code is the tested code."
